WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.490
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.900
Style transfer is an interesting problem in
machine learning research where we have two

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:15.099
input images, one for content, and one for
style, and the output is our content image

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:17.570
reimagined with this new style.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:23.189
The cool part is that the content can be a
photo straight from our camera, and the style

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:28.070
can be a painting, which leads to super fun,
and really good looking results.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:33.640
This subfield is only a few years old and
has seen a number of amazing papers - style

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:40.280
transfer for HD images, videos, and some of
these forgeries were even able to make professional

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.310
art curators think that they were painted
by a real artist.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:50.850
So, here is a crazy idea -- how about using
style transfer to create caricatures?

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.019
Well, this sounds quite challenging.

00:00:54.019 --> 00:01:00.239
Just think about it - a caricature is an elusive
art where certain human features are exaggerated,

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:05.449
and generally, the human face needs to be
simplified and boiled down into its essence.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:08.310
It is a very human thing to do.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:14.259
So how could possibly an AI be endowed with
such a deep understanding of, for instance,

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:15.960
a human face?

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.270
That sounds almost impossible.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:23.049
Our suspicion is further reinforced as we
look at how previous style transfer algorithms

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.310
try to deal with this problem.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.520
Not too well, but no wonder, it would be unfair
to expect great results as this is not what

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.010
they were designed for.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:37.440
But now, look at these truly incredible results
that were made with this new work.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.649
The main difference between the older works
and this one is that one, it uses generative

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:45.790
adversarial networks, GANs in short.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:51.440
This is an architecture where two neural networks
learn together -- one learns to generate better

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.719
forgeries, and the other learns to find out
whether an image has been forged.

00:01:56.719 --> 00:02:00.360
However, this would still not create the results
that you see here.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:05.340
An additional improvement is that we have
not one, but two of these GANs.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.280
One deals with style.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.720
But, it is trained in a way to keep the essence
of the image.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:17.350
And the other deals with changing and warping
the geometry of the image to achieve an artistic

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.430
effect.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:24.050
This leans on the input of a landmark detector
that gives it around 60 points that show the

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:27.130
location of the most important parts of a
human face.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:32.120
The output of this geometry GAN is a distorted
version of this point set, which can then

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.620
be used to warp the style image to obtain
the final output.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:42.460
This is a great idea because the amount of
distortion applied to the points can be controlled.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:49.390
So, we can tell the AI how crazy of a result
we are looking for.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.390
Great!

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.420
The authors also experimented applying this
to video.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.290
In my opinion, the results are incredible
for a first crack at this problem.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:05.530
We are probably just one paper away from an
AI automatically creating absolutely mind

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.620
blowing caricature videos.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.250
Make sure to have a look at the paper as it
has a ton more results and of course, every

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.170
element of the system is explained in great
detail there.

